1
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:42,000
On the Eastern front in 1943, the German soldiers no longer had any ideals.
They were not fighting for the Party—but for their lives!

2
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:18,000
Cross of Iron is a drama, action, history film directed by Sam Peckinpah.

3
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:54,000
It is 1943, and the German army—ravaged and demoralised—is
hastily retreating from the Russian front.

4
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:30,000
In the midst of the madness, conflict brews between the aristocratic yet ultimately
pusillanimous Captain Stransky and the courageous Corporal Steiner.

5
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:06,000
Stransky is the only man who believes that the Third Reich is
still vastly superior to the Russian army.

6
00:39:36,000 --> 00:39:42,000
However, within his pompous persona lies a quivering coward who longs for
the Iron Cross so that he can return to Berlin a hero.

7
00:46:12,000 --> 00:46:18,000
Steiner, on the other hand is cynical, defiantly non-conformist and more concerned with the safety of his
own men rather than the horde of military decorations offered to him by his superiors.

8
00:52:48,000 --> 00:52:54,000
Unteroffizier / Feldwebel Rolf Steiner, played by James Coburn.

9
00:59:24,000 --> 00:59:30,000
Hauptmann Stransky, played by Maximilian Schell.

10
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
Oberst Brandt, played by James Mason.

11
01:12:36,000 --> 01:12:42,000
Hauptmann Kiesel, played by David Warner.

12
01:19:12,000 --> 01:19:18,000
Unteroffizier Krüger, played by Klaus Löwitsch.

13
01:25:48,000 --> 01:25:54,000
Gefreiter Kern, played by Vadim Glowna.

14
01:32:24,000 --> 01:32:30,000
Cross of Iron (German: Steiner – Das Eiserne Kreuz, lit.

15
01:39:00,000 --> 01:39:06,000
"Steiner – The Iron Cross") is a 1977 war film directed by Sam Peckinpah,
featuring James Coburn, Maximilian Schell, James Mason, and David Warner.

16
01:45:36,000 --> 01:45:42,000
Set on the Eastern Front in World War II during the Soviets' Caucasus operations against the German Kuban bridgehead on the Taman Peninsula in late 1943, the film focuses
on the class conflict between a newly arrived, aristocratic Prussian officer who covets winning the Iron Cross and a cynical, battle-hardened infantry NCO.

17
01:52:12,000 --> 01:52:18,000
An international co-production between British and West German financiers,
the film's exteriors were shot on location in Yugoslavia.

18
01:58:48,000 --> 01:58:54,000
The film explores themes of hostility, world war ii,
battle for power, troops, commander.

19
02:05:24,000 --> 02:05:30,000
The tone is emotional.
